WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:01.220 --> 00:08.100
Today, Aaliyah has invited Noah to a meeting to introduce herself as Chief Transformation Officer.

2
00:09.160 --> 00:15.300
Aaliyah wants to discuss how she, Noah and the Digital department are going to collaborate

3
00:15.650 --> 00:17.950
to ensure a successful transformation.

4
00:18.890 --> 00:19.970
What’s next on the agenda?

5
00:21.250 --> 00:22.270
My meeting with Aaliyah.

6
00:23.210 --> 00:24.190
What’s this about again?

7
00:26.310 --> 00:28.030
Right — the transformation.

8
00:28.810 --> 00:29.250
Ugh.

9
00:29.890 --> 00:34.210
Last time we had a transformation, my team wasn’t happy.

10
00:35.010 --> 00:37.860
She already has some hard deadlines in mind.

11
00:38.530 --> 00:41.220
Ahh! I am so hungry!

12
00:41.640 --> 00:44.670
Why on earth do people schedule meetings at lunchtime?

13
00:45.890 --> 00:48.030
Okay, I have a meeting with Noah soon.

14
00:48.450 --> 00:50.910
I can’t wait to have some extra brain power on this.

15
00:51.720 --> 00:55.159
Oh, everything’s starting to catch up with me these days.

16
00:55.159 --> 01:00.710
My personal training, the women’s mentorship initiative, my local youth group — and now this

17
01:01.130 --> 01:02.110
transformation.

18
01:03.330 --> 01:04.420
Aaliyah, stop!

19
01:05.350 --> 01:05.920
Breathe.

20
01:06.440 --> 01:08.420
Remember what your meditation app tells you to do.

21
01:09.060 --> 01:10.750
Breathe in the positive energy.

22
01:11.750 --> 01:13.250
Breathe out the negative energy.

23
01:13.990 --> 01:15.650
I’m confident my team can make this work.

24
01:16.420 --> 01:18.240
Aaliyah! How are you?

25
01:18.920 --> 01:21.604
Oh, hey! Oops — let me get these crumbs off my desk.

26
01:21.604 --> 01:24.960
I’m so sorry, I promise I don’t usually have meetings over lunch.

27
01:25.540 --> 01:27.070
No worries.

28
01:27.400 --> 01:29.410
Oof, it’s been one of those days, Noah.

29
01:29.990 --> 01:31.256
Thank you for being flexible.

30
01:31.256 --> 01:35.360
You know, I realised I’ve been here five years and I’ve never had the chance to work with you.

31
01:36.040 --> 01:38.370
I know! Kind of hard to believe.

32
01:38.980 --> 01:40.770
I bet we’ll make a great team.

33
01:41.510 --> 01:46.882
Absolutely. So I wanted to take some time before our full team kick-off to get to know each other a little better.

34
01:46.882 --> 01:52.160
We’ll be working closely together, so I really want us to have a clear sense of our roles in the transformation.

35
01:52.710 --> 01:55.460
Anything else that you think would be helpful for us to talk about today?

36
01:56.420 --> 02:02.150
Well, it would be helpful if you just share your plan and deadlines so my team can keep up with you.

37
02:02.890 --> 02:04.550
Then I’ll know whether we can deliver.

38
02:05.930 --> 02:08.290
You can’t say that.

39
02:09.060 --> 02:13.310
Aaliyah looks like she’s in a tight spot right now with everything that’s been going on.

40
02:13.890 --> 02:18.470
Starting off on the right track means putting yourself in the other person’s shoes.

41
02:19.330 --> 02:22.050
What are they thinking and feeling? And why?

42
02:22.790 --> 02:24.130
What is at stake for them?

43
02:25.290 --> 02:30.898
Taking the time before and during your conversation to recognise where someone is coming from

44
02:30.898 --> 02:33.310
can help you meet them where they stand.

45
02:34.280 --> 02:38.400
To be honest, Aaliyah, it would be great to start off by learning more about you.

46
02:39.210 --> 02:40.710
How are you feeling in the new role?

47
02:41.410 --> 02:43.520
I bet you’ve got a lot on your plate right now.

48
02:44.490 --> 02:48.148
I know — I didn’t expect the transformation to kick off this early,

49
02:48.148 --> 02:51.970
so I’m trying to wrap up a bunch of different things on my to-do list.

50
02:52.900 --> 02:53.700
Aaliyah,

51
02:55.170 --> 02:56.030
you’re not alone.

52
02:56.550 --> 02:58.850
You have a great team here to support you.

53
03:00.680 --> 03:01.350
But you know what?

54
03:02.050 --> 03:04.230
Let’s go introduce you to the rest of the team.

